 thing  is normal customers and normal average  people don't know that it's a high-end  phone the average person watching that  presentation doesn't know that it's an  octa-core processor overseas an  eight-core cpu the average person  doesn't know it has 2 gigabytes of RAM  and that's partially because Samsung  never actually said that they never even  said that it ran Android during the  presentation they saved all that for the  very end and a final slide after the  final credits that give the  full specs of the device so the fact  that it's a high-end hardware device  isn't really a big deal to Samsung why  is that that's because they're not  selling hardware anymore and it may  sound weird to say that but Samsung is  actually now selling or at least adding  value to their devices via software not  hardware they sold a lot of things based  on software and features not really  based on oh this has an 8 megapixel  camera I want to buy that no one is  buying the s3 for that reason people are  buying the s3 because it has Samsung  features and Samsung said well I think  we can expand on that with the Galaxy s4  so basically Samsung has seen that  adding value via software not hardware  is doing really well at getting and  attracting customers now the average  person may actually look at the  processor and say oh wow that's an 8  core processor that seems like it's a  great idea but for the most part they  don't flip out over those things they  don't flip out over the fact that it has  2 gigabytes of RAM or the fact that it  has Android 4.2 versus 4.1 they look at  the fact that you can turn the page  without touching the screen and they  freak out over things like that software  features that that you can look at other  phones and say well that phone can't do  that  I want the one that you can do magic  tricks with that seems like a really  cool phone to buy unload a link in the  description right below the like button  that has basically Samsung's wrap-up or  overvi