ll allow you to do video chat using  both cameras or screen sharing using the  chat service there's also s translator  which does exactly what google  translator does live but it's just s  translator now you also have s voice  which we've seen already is the same  thing as Google now - the predictive  search but it's now Samsung based so you  have the S theme going on here and you  also have s health which is a monitor of  your physical health goals so if you  look at all these things that Samsung is  putting together it's pretty obvious  that there is a ton of s stuff and  Samsung stuff and they just named all of  the things they named everything they  possibly can to give it a name that  people will remember it's a feature that  they are trying to sell not a hardware  thing but a software thing and because  it is software pretty much all these  things are also going to be available in  an update of the galaxy s3 and the  galaxy note 2 now we tech people were of  course rolling our eyes when Samsung  spent half an hour showing how we could  swipe from tab to tab in the web browser  without touching the screen but that  wasn't for us that wasn't for the couple  hundred thousand tech people watching  that was for the people the average  people who actually have never seen that  happen before on any device and think  wow can the Sony Spurrier's e do that no  can the Oppo find five do that No  i phone do that no so I think I want  this coin instead usually we don't  really consider these features important  but then some of us tech people actually  think you know they actually ask the  question if I root this device and put  CyanogenMod on it am I going to lose  that s-pen feature am I going to lose  that airView feature so it's actually  becoming more important to us so the  Samsung S features and s stuff is  actually getting to us now and it's  becoming a thing that we associate with  the galaxy brand and the galaxy hardware  now all the software based enhancements  